{% comment %}
  Outputs the handle of the collection that represents an ARTWORK product's
  artist, or nothing when there is no match. Capture it and look the collection
  up in the caller:

    {%- capture ah -%}{%- render 'rb-artist-handle', product: product -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign ah = ah | strip -%}
    {%- assign artist_col = collections[ah] -%}

  The sibling of snippets/rb-teacher-handle.liquid, and it exists for the same
  reason: one product template serves every artwork, so the link through to the
  artist's page has to be resolved from the product rather than from a
  per-page setting.

  This store models an artist as a collection holding that artist's works, so
  the product already belongs to it. The artist's NAME is the product vendor.

  Never handleize the vendor to guess the URL. "Zara-Leigh Farinha" handleizes
  to zara-leigh-farinha, which is a stale collection — her real artist page is
  zara-leigh. The catalogue is inconsistent in the other direction too
  ("Shelly" vs "Shelley" Cowling), so the match is made through a collection
  the product is actually in, comparing titles, and falling back to the
  surname the way the teacher lookup does.

  Two collections can share one title: a person who both teaches and exhibits
  has the teacher one under a "-1" handle beside the artist one. Here the
  artist page is wanted, so "-1" is the LAST resort rather than the tie-break —
  the exact inverse of rb-teacher-handle.

  Collections that are catalogue machinery rather than people are skipped, or
  "gallery" would win on nearly every artwork.

  Accepts: product.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign vendor = product.vendor | downcase | strip
  assign name_parts = vendor | split: ' '
  assign surname = name_parts | last

  comment
    Smart and system collections every artwork also belongs to. Kept as one
    comma-joined string so a single `contains` test covers the lot; each entry
    is comma-wrapped so "artists" never matches inside another handle.
  endcomment
  assign skip = ',gallery,all,frontpage,art-under,art-quiz,wishlist,warm-tones,cool-tones,neutral-tones,originals,limited-editions,artists,teachers,classes,workshops,workshops-classes,classes-workshops,workshops-and-classes,'

  assign found = ''
  assign twin = ''
  assign fallback = ''

  for c in product.collections
    assign probe = ',' | append: c.handle | append: ','
    if skip contains probe
      continue
    endif

    assign ct = c.title | downcase | strip
    assign hit = false
    if vendor != blank
      if ct == vendor
        assign hit = true
      elsif surname != blank and ct contains surname
        assign hit = true
      endif
    endif

    assign tail = c.handle | slice: -2, 2

    if hit
      if tail == '-1'
        if twin == blank
          assign twin = c.handle
        endif
      elsif found == blank
        assign found = c.handle
      endif
    elsif fallback == blank
      assign fallback = c.handle
    endif
  endfor

  comment
    Order of confidence: a title match on a non-teacher handle, then the
    teacher twin (still the right person), then any collection the piece is in
    that is not catalogue machinery.
  endcomment
  if found == blank
    assign found = twin
  endif
  if found == blank
    assign found = fallback
  endif

  echo found
-%}
